The question is for the cumulative surface dose to a tissue imaged with a multiple energy imaging system. D1 is the dose booked on one monochromatic Laue pass. A Laue multiple-energy imager does not irradiate a given surface point once; the same raster point is illuminated once for each Laue energy used in the material-decomposition acquisition and the kerma adds incoherently:

D_cum\simeq N_E D_1.

For the canonical dual-energy K-edge / material-decomposition implementation N_E=2, ... D_2\simeq2D_1\approx7.8\;\mu{\rm Gy}
